## EY Financial Report for 2020: A Comprehensive Research Report

**Executive Summary:**

EY reported global revenues of US$37.2 billion in 2020, demonstrating resilience amidst a challenging global landscape.  This report analyzes EY's financial performance in 2020, leveraging publicly available information including their illustrative financial statements, transparency report, and news releases.  The report also delves into key concepts related to EY's business, recent developments, applications of their services, future outlook, and the merits and demerits of their operations.  While a consolidated financial statement from EY itself for 2020 is not publicly accessible, this report utilizes illustrative statements and other disclosed information to provide a comprehensive overview. (Links: https://www.ey.com/en_gl/newsroom/2020/09/ey-reports-global-revenues-of-us-37-2b-in-2020, https://www.ey.com/en_gl/technical/ifrs-technical-resources/good-group-international-limited-illustrative-consolidated-financial-statements-december-2020, https://www.ey.com/content/dam/ey-unified-site/ey-com/en-la/documents/ey-lao-fy20-transparency-report.pdf)


**Introduction:**

Ernst & Young (EY) is a multinational professional services network and one of the Big Four accounting firms.  Their services encompass assurance, consulting, strategy and transactions, and tax. Understanding their financial performance is crucial for stakeholders, including clients, investors, and the broader business community.  This report aims to provide a detailed analysis of EY's financial standing in 2020, drawing upon publicly available resources. (Link: https://www.ey.com/en_gl/newsroom/2020/09/ey-reports-global-revenues-of-us-37-2b-in-2020)


**Key Concepts:**

EY's business model revolves around providing professional services to a diverse client base. Key concepts include:

* **Assurance:** Independent audits of financial statements.
* **Consulting:** Advisory services across various domains, including technology, strategy, and operations.
* **Strategy and Transactions:**  Supporting mergers, acquisitions, and other corporate transactions.
* **Tax:** Tax compliance, planning, and advisory services.
* **Global Network:**  Operating through a network of member firms worldwide.


**Recent Developments:**

In 2020, EY reported global revenues of US$37.2 billion.  The firm also faced scrutiny related to audit quality, as highlighted in the PCAOB inspection report. (Links: https://www.ey.com/en_gl/newsroom/2020/09/ey-reports-global-revenues-of-us-37-2b-in-2020, https://assets.pcaobus.org/pcaob-dev/docs/default-source/inspections/reports/documents/104-2021-151-ey.pdf?sfvrsn=2c8cadd5_4)


**Applications:**

EY's services are applicable to a wide range of industries and organizations, including:

* **Large Corporations:**  Auditing, consulting, and tax services.
* **Government Entities:**  Public sector consulting and advisory.
* **Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs):**  Growth and operational support.


**Future Outlook:**

EY continues to invest in emerging technologies, such as AI, to enhance its service offerings and cater to evolving client needs.  The provided PDF documents highlight EY's commitment to creating long-term value for clients by leveraging AI and its involvement with the WEF-IBC Stakeholder Capitalism Metrics. (Links: https://www.ey.com/en_gl/value-realized-annual-report, https://www.ey.com/content/dam/ey-unified-site/ey-com/en-gl/campaigns/value-realized/documents/ey-gl-value-realized-report-client-value-10-2024.pdf, https://www.ey.com/content/dam/ey-unified-site/ey-com/en-gl/campaigns/value-realized/documents/ey-gl-wef-ibc-metrics-10-2024.pdf)  Further, EY's values, outlined in the provided PDF, emphasize integrity, respect, and inclusiveness. (https://www.ey.com/content/dam/ey-unified-site/ey-com/en-gl/campaigns/value-realized/documents/ey-gl-purpose-values-strategy-10-2024.pdf)


**Merits and Demerits:**

**Merits:**  Global reach, comprehensive service portfolio, brand recognition.

**Demerits:**  Potential conflicts of interest, scrutiny related to audit quality, competition from other Big Four firms.


**Conclusion:**

EY's 2020 financial performance reflected its position as a leading professional services firm. While the firm navigated challenges related to audit quality and a dynamic global environment, its revenue figures demonstrated resilience.  EY's ongoing investments in technology and commitment to client value position it for continued growth in the future.  This report provides a valuable overview of EY's 2020 financial year, leveraging the available public information.  Access to a full, audited financial statement would enhance the depth of analysis and provide further insight into EY's overall financial health.